// Type-checking-only config (NOT used by the rollup build). Run via `npm run typecheck`.
// Mirrors the base tsconfig (loose: noImplicitAny:false, strict off) but scoped to
// src/ with skipLibCheck, so it's a clean green/red compile signal — exits 0 today.
//
// This is the ratchet for the ongoing `any`-removal work: it catches mistakes on
// values that DO have real types (wrong field, type incompat, etc.) — exactly what
// we add when we replace an `any`. It does NOT enforce full strict.
//
// NOTE: full `strict` currently surfaces ~3786 errors (dominated by property-access
// on the decaffeinated object-literal singletons + null-safety), so strict is a
// large future burndown, not a freebie. noImplicitAny:false is load-bearing here.
//
// Scoped to src/ — tools/ has its own tools/tsconfig.json (node16 + @types/node).
// fbegin.js/fend.js are intentionally-invalid dead build fragments, excluded.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": [
    "src/meta/fbegin.js",
    "src/meta/fend.js"
  ]
}
